title: Government of National Unity
subtitle: Trevannon's solution to the impasse?
view-if: chancellor == "Trevannon" and treviranus_post and next_reichstag_time == rubicon_time and next_reichstag_time > 0 and year == 1934
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
tags: event
go-to: treviranus_menu

= Government of National Unity

Trevannon, having failed to win over the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**CSG**</span>, has now turned to us for support. We find ourselves in the role of kingmaker, while the Chancellor grows increasingly desperate to secure a majority. However, DuFour—on his death bed—lacks the energy to intervene in the process, leading Trevannon to personally approach us with an offer.

He is offering to repeal the ban on the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if sapd_formed:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span>?], in return for us refraining to call a vote of no confidence on his government until DuFour inevitably kicks the bucket.

But perhaps we can bypass this deadlock by targeting DuFour himself. With a two-thirds majority in the Assembly, we could initiate impeachment proceedings, or trigger a recall election, under the Unity Constitution. If the recall election were to fail, the Assembly would be dissolved for new elections.

Yet the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> nature of the courts renders impeachment unlikely to succeed. Recall, however, remains a narrow possibility—it requires only a majority of those who vote, not of all eligible voters. Still, to make either path viable, we must secure the backing of other parties.

@treviranus_menu

- @reichstag
- @reichstag_impeach

@reichstag_impeach
title: Put forth a motion to remove President DuFour from office.
subtitle: A two-thirds majority in the Assembly is required to succeed.
on-arrival: {!
Q.impeachment_votes = 0;

Q.impeachment_votes += Q.marcher_r;
Q.impeachment_votes += Q.collectivist_r;
if (Q.sapd_r) Q.impeachment_votes += Q.sapd_r;
if (!Q.lvp_formed) {
  Q.impeachment_votes += Q.ddp_r;
  Q.impeachment_ddp = 1;
}
if (Q.gold_ideology != "Right" && Q.gold_exist && !Q.lvp_formed) { 
  Q.impeachment_votes += Q.gold_r;
  Q.impeachment_gold = 1;
}
if (Q.lvp_formed) { 
  Q.impeachment_votes += Q.lvp_r;
  Q.impeachment_lvp = 1;
}
if (Q.unionist_relation >= 25) {
  Q.impeachment_votes += Q.unionist_r - Q.bvp_r;
  Q.impeachment_unionist = 1;
}
if (Q.unionist_relation >= 35) {
  Q.impeachment_votes += Q.bvp_r;
  Q.impeachment_bvp = 1;
}
Q.impeachment_votes += Q.royalist_gallax_r;
if (Q.nvf_exist) Q.impeachment_votes += Q.nvf_r

Q.impeachment_votes = parseFloat(Q.impeachment_votes.toFixed(1));
!}
max-visits: 1

We are able to gather the support of [+ marcher_r + collectivist_r + sapd_r +]% of the Assembly, with all <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if sapd_formed:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span>?] deputies expected to vote in favor. Our effort is also aided by the fact that DuFour only has a few months left to live.

[? if impeachment_ddp: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has been one of the only propertied parties standing up for the Unity Republic and the constitution the party's founders drafted. We are expected to see their deputies vote with us. ?][? if not impeachment_ddp and not lvp_formed: Unfortunately, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has strayed too far from its former <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> ideals, and now sees support for DuFour as a hard but necessary choice in the national interest. ?]

[? if impeachment_gold: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> were once staunch supporters of DuFour, but even the guild-masters have grown tired of his antics and have lobbied the party to vote against the president. ?][? if not impeachment_gold and not lvp_formed and gold_exist: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> remains trapped in its <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> spiral and will not support our motion. ?]

[? if impeachment_lvp: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, nominally a <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> party, has remained faithful to its democratic convictions and will vote against President DuFour. ?][? if not impeachment_lvp and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> has drifted far from its professed <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> and democratic principles. Swayed by its <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> right wing, it will reluctantly remain aligned with DuFour. ?]

[? if impeachment_unionist: The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, our ally since the Republic’s founding, stands with us to defend it. ?][? if not impeachment_unionist: The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, our ally since the Republic’s founding, has unexpectedly sided with DuFour. Strained relations are to blame, as they now prioritize the survival of Trevannon’s government over principle. ?]

[? if impeachment_bvp: Even the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span>—once deeply loyal to DuFour—has grown disillusioned with his anti-constitutionalist and erratic behavior, and now supports our effort. ?][? if not impeachment_bvp: The <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> has, as expected, remained loyal to President DuFour, despite their reported discontent over his anti-constitutional conduct. ?]

The right-wing parties and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> remain DuFour’s most loyal supporters. Even Mallin recognizes the danger of a potential <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> president should DuFour be removed from office.

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>[? if nvf_exist:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #142e20;">**NPF**</span>?] will break with the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**CSG**</span> on the vote, and vote to impeach the president that has impeded their progress over and over again.

- @reichstag_impeach_2
- @reichstag_impeach_fail

@reichstag_impeach_2
title: The moment of truth...
unavailable-subtitle: The Assembly can simply relegate our motion down the agenda.
choose-if: impeachment_votes >= 50
go-to: reichstag_impeach_3 if impeachment_votes >= 66.7; reichstag_impeach_fail_2 if impeachment_votes < 66.7

With a simple majority, the Assembly has chosen to set aside our motion and instead proceed with a vote of no confidence in Trevannon first. Should the motion pass—as is likely—his government will collapse, and the Assembly will likely be either adjourned or dissolved in the aftermath.

@reichstag_impeach_3
on-arrival: {!
Q.reichstag_break = 1;
Q.dufour_explode = 1;

Q.impeachment_ref_week = Q.week + 4;
Q.impeachment_ref_month = Q.month;
Q.impeachment_ref_year = Q.year;
Q.impeachment_ref_time = Q.rubicon_time + 4;

let added_months = Math.floor(Q.impeachment_ref_week / 4);
Q.impeachment_ref_month += added_months;
Q.impeachment_ref_week = Q.impeachment_ref_week % 4;
if (Q.impeachment_ref_week === 0) Q.impeachment_ref_week = 1;

if (Q.impeachment_ref_month > 12) {
    Q.impeachment_ref_month -= 12;
    Q.impeachment_ref_year += 1;
}
!}

[+ impeachment_votes +]% of the Assembly has voted to recall President DuFour! But our fight is not over yet. A popular referendum is scheduled exactly one month from now to confirm the Assembly’s decision.

If the referendum succeeds, a new presidential election will be held to determine DuFour’s successor. But if it fails, the constitution mandates that the Assembly be dissolved and fresh elections called once again.

The referendum is scheduled for [+ impeachment_ref_month : month +] [+ impeachment_ref_year +], Week [+ impeachment_ref_week +].

@reichstag_impeach_fail
title: The Assembly shoots down our motion.
subtitle: An anti-climatic end.
view-if: impeachment_votes < 50
go-to: treviranus_menu

With a simple majority, the Assembly has chosen to set aside our motion. We must decide on the deal next.

@reichstag_impeach_fail_2
go-to: treviranus_menu

Despite our best efforts, we manage to rally only [+ impeachment_votes +]% of the Assembly to our cause. We must decide on the deal next.

@reichstag
title: We can certainly wait a few months, accept the deal.
subtitle: The Commonwealth parliamentary system desperately needs legitimacy. Forcing new elections now risks driving voters further into the extremes.
on-arrival: collectivist_banned = 0; sapd_banned = 0; vanguard_strength += 30; commons_collectivist += 6; disfavored_collectivist += 6; commons_sapd += 2; disfavored_sapd += 2; pro_republic += 10

Under the influence of the plot and the modman's laziness, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> has agreed on a truce, and Trevannon survives another day. DuFour is reportedly displeased at this development, but doesn't intervene as expected. He must be really sick then.